/* vr_core.js v1: WebXR for the BSA (couple3d.html) and the Atelier. A CLASSIC script on the global THREE (r128), shared by both pages.
   Built for a Meta Quest (Ruth 2026-10-06): hand tracking or controllers, pinch / trigger = grab. Served as http://localhost:8188 through `adb reverse tcp:8188 tcp:8188`
   (localhost is a secure context, so WebXR works with no certificate and nothing is exposed). See VR_QUEST_SETUP.html next to this file.

   A page calls VRCore.mount({
       renderer, scene, camera,                      the page's own
       frame(),                                      runs one page frame (the page's loop body); in XR it is called once, then it keeps itself going through the rAF queue below
       beforeEnter(), afterExit(),                   optional: the page drops bloom/shadows for XR (EffectComposer does not run in XR) and puts them back
       handles(),                                    [{id, pos:THREE.Vector3 (world), color?:0xRRGGBB}] the joints that can be grabbed now
       grab:{ begin(id,tip,head)->bool, move(tip,head), end() },   the page's own IK drag (couple3d drives its real pointer pipeline, so hinge limits, pins and undo stay the app's)
       objects(),                                    [{id,name,object:THREE.Object3D}] bodies and props for Move, Turn and Size
       undo:{ push(), undo(), redo() },
       save()->Promise, scenes()->[{id,name}], openScene(id),
       clip:{ play(), pause(), keep() }              optional
   })
   Nothing is read from page globals. No flashing: handles do not pulse, the camera never moves without her input (snap turn, the Life size / Tabletop buttons, Leave).
   prefers-reduced-motion: opts.freeze(true) is called on enter. */
