/* ---------- the control browser, dressed like the page (Ruth 2026-10-07: same icons, same colours, same places in both apps) ----------
   It MIRRORS the page's own controls: the page tells it which toolbar icons (a left rail, in the page's own order and groups, with the same flyouts) and which
   panels to offer (opts.controls()). Every row is a real button, tick box, slider or list from that page; pointing and pinching presses the real element (a click,
   or the real value and its input event), so a control behaves exactly as on the computer. Tiles can be dragged to a new place; the order is remembered. */
